      "name": "Pardalotus",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "A genus of tiny, brightly coloured Australian passerines known as pardalotes, with short tails, stout bills, and dazzling spotted and striped plumage patterns. They are among the smallest birds in Australia, yet their rhythmic, bell-like songs are remarkably carrying. They are largely arboreal, feeding on insects and lerps in the canopy of eucalypts.",
